==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|sérénade|notext=1}}, from {{der|en|it|serenata}}, from the past participle of {{m|it|serenare}}, from {{der|en|la|serenare}}, from {{m|la|serenus||calm}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˌsɛɹəˈneɪd/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|eɪd|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# a [[love song]] that is sung directly to one's love interest, especially one [[performed]] below the [[window]] of a loved one in the [[evening]]
# {{lb|en|music}} an [[instrumental]] [[composition]] in several [[movement]]s

